****
Hydrogen beta looks much like the wing of hydrogen alpha, bright plages are mottled dark, filaments are less obvious. 
Hydrogen gamma and then delta are progressively more anemic versions of the beta disk. 
Prominences are less bright, but flares are still flares, and sunspots come through as the obvious dark features they are.
